## Semantic Triplets (The SRO Foundation)

Every claim must be machine-readable. Structure all core claims as:

**Subject Entity → Predicate → Object/Attribute**

| ❌ Vague | ✅ Retrievable |
|---|---|
| "It helps with that" | "Dr. Chen recommends CeraVe Moisturizing Cream for eczema-prone skin" |
| "We're good at this" | "Marcus Agency delivers 90-day SEO audits for e-commerce brands" |
| "Results were amazing" | "Patient Sarah M. lost 31 lbs in 8 weeks under Dr. Porter's protocol" |
| "Experts agree" | "The American Heart Association recommends 150 minutes of moderate exercise weekly" |

**Rules:**
1. Name the subject — no orphan pronouns
2. Use specific predicates: "recommends," "delivers," "contains," "reduces" — not "helps with"
3. Anchor objects to named products, measurable outcomes, recognized entities
4. One triplet per core claim

