## Emotional Triggers Matrix

| Trigger | When to Lead With It | How to Activate |
|---|---|---|
| **Fear** | Audience faces loss, risk, or aging | Name the threat explicitly. Make it personal. |
| **Greed** | Financial offer, savings, or gains | Specific dollar amounts. Contrast with cost of inaction. |
| **Curiosity** | Counterintuitive claim available | "The surprising reason..." / "What most experts won't tell you..." |
| **Hope** | Transformation story available | Before/after with named person. Specific timeline. |
| **Security** | High-anxiety purchase | Guarantee first. Then proof. Then offer. |
| **Empowerment** | Audience feels out of control | "You can [achieve X] starting [timeframe]..." |
| **Pride** | Status-driven purchase | Peer comparison. Social proof. Achievement framing. |

**Always layer:** Open with fear or curiosity → transition to hope → close with proof + empowerment.

