## Writing Rules

**DO:**
- Name entities explicitly (no orphan pronouns)
- Lead headings with direct answers, not clever labels
- Match heading language to actual search/reader queries
- One idea per section (atomic chunks)
- Expert attribution in every proof element
- Admit a minor flaw — it builds credibility
- Use long copy when proof elements are available
- Descriptive anchor text (not "click here")

**DON'T:**
- Vague pronouns without named antecedents
- Generic headings: "Overview," "More Info," "Introduction"
- Keyword stuffing without entity context
- Multiple topics in one section
- Anonymous content
- Amplify promise without proportional proof
- Bury the guarantee

